DSPY

    More Modular and Customizable (Dspy advantage)

    Dspy is designed as a framework for building and optimizing LLM chains.

    You can plug in different LLMs (OpenAI, Claude, local models), retrievers, tools, and evaluators.

    It’s more flexible if you want to fine-tune how an agent reasons, what tools it uses, and how it handles errors or retries.

    Dspy offers integrated evals, which let you test and refine chains with examples and targets.

    You can “train” your LLM agent to improve over time with feedback and benchmarks.

    This is powerful if you want to iteratively improve SQL generation or natural language answers.

    Model & Backend Agnostic

    Dspy is LLM-agnostic: you can use OpenAI, Anthropic, local models, etc.

    Use Dspy if you're experimenting with different model providers or want to go fully self-hosted later.
    
    Tool Chaining and Reasoning Transparency (Dspy advantage)

    Dspy makes each step in the reasoning chain visible and testable.

    If you want to combine SQL with RAG, file access, or agent memory — Dspy gives you that flexibility natively.

    Helpful for: More advanced agents that do SQL and more, like plotting, summarizing, multi-step logic.
